Monetization Section > CustomersDot engineering > Deployment
CustomersDot uses continuous deployment. Merges to staging deploy to staging, run E2E tests, and auto deploy to production after 3 hours.
graph TD;
    A(Merged) --> |Green tests| B(Staging);
    B --> C[E2E tests on staging];
    C --> D[Verification];
    D --> E(Auto deploy to production in 3 hours);
- To stop a production deploy, open a non-confidential issue with the production::blocker label.
- To expedite a fix while a blocker is in place, unschedule the production job and trigger it manually after removing the label.
- Use feature flags for significant changes.
- Feature freeze matches the rest of GitLab, from the Friday the milestone ends to release day.

Engineering Workflow > CI Health incidents {#broken-master} > Merging while an incident is open {#merging-during-broken-master}
If your pipeline fails only because of an open CI Health incident, wait for the fix rather than working around it. Merge trains build on top of the default branch, so an unrelated merge can add new failures and make the incident harder to track down. Don't bypass the failure unless the situation is urgent.
When the situation is urgent, there is an exception.

